  "helpTitle": "Help & Guide",
  "welcomeToFarrierLog": "Welcome to FarrierLog",
  "helpIntro": "This guide walks through everything FarrierLog can do, from adding your first client to backing up your data. Tap a section below to expand it.",
  "helpSectionGettingStartedTitle": "Getting Started",
  "helpStepGettingStarted1": "Open Settings and fill in your company name, address, phone, and email — this appears on every invoice you send.",
  "helpStepGettingStarted2": "Pick a color theme and set your preferred currency and distance unit.",
  "helpStepGettingStarted3": "Add your first client from the Clients tab, then add their animals.",
  "helpStepGettingStarted4": "Schedule a visit from the client's page or the calendar's new appointment button.",
  "helpSectionClientsAnimalsTitle": "Clients & Animals",
  "helpStepClientsAnimals1": "Go to the Clients tab and tap the add button to create a new client with their contact details and address.",
  "helpStepClientsAnimals2": "Open a client's page and tap \"Add Animal\" to add each horse or other animal you service for them.",
  "helpStepClientsAnimals3": "Tap a client's phone number to call, or long-press it to text.",
  "helpStepClientsAnimals4": "Tap a client's address to open it in maps for directions.",
  "helpStepClientsAnimals5": "Use \"Internal Notes\" on a client or animal for private staff notes — these never appear on invoices.",
  "helpStepClientsAnimals6": "Swipe left on a client or animal to delete it. Deleting a client also deletes their animals, visits, and photos.",
  "helpSectionSchedulingTitle": "Scheduling Visits",
  "helpStepScheduling1": "Tap the calendar tab to see all upcoming and past visits — solid markers are confirmed, outlined markers are auto-generated projections.",
  "helpStepScheduling2": "Tap the new appointment button on the calendar to schedule a visit on a specific date.",
  "helpStepScheduling3": "Search for a client by name or address instead of scrolling a long list.",
  "helpStepScheduling4": "Set a recurrence interval (in weeks) on a visit to automatically project the next appointment once you confirm the current one.",
  "helpStepScheduling5": "Confirming an auto-generated visit creates the next projected visit in the chain — future visits are not created all at once.",
  "helpSectionInvoicingTitle": "Services, Charges & Invoicing",
  "helpStepInvoicing1": "Open a visit and add service lines for each animal — enter a description and price, or billing by headcount for group services.",
  "helpStepInvoicing2": "Save frequently used services as templates in Settings so you can add them with one tap next time.",
  "helpStepInvoicing3": "Add travel and incidental charges (mileage, tolls, reimbursements) separately from service lines.",
  "helpStepInvoicing4": "Set your default mileage rate in Settings so it's pre-filled every time you add a travel charge.",
  "helpStepInvoicing5": "When a visit is complete, generate the invoice PDF, then print or share it directly from the visit.",
  "helpSectionGettingPaidTitle": "Getting Paid",
  "helpStepGettingPaid1": "A visit has two states: completed (work is done) and paid (payment received) — mark each as it happens.",
  "helpStepGettingPaid2": "The dashboard shows earned and projected revenue so you can track what's outstanding at a glance.",
  "helpStepGettingPaid3": "Use the invoice history screen to find and re-share any past invoice.",
  "helpStepGettingPaid4": "Unpaid, past-due visits are highlighted so nothing slips through.",
  "helpSectionPhotosTitle": "Photos",
  "helpStepPhotos1": "From a visit, capture photos and tag them to one or more animals using the checkboxes — all animals on the visit are pre-checked by default.",
  "helpStepPhotos2": "Open an animal's detail page to see its full photo history, oldest first, with the elapsed time between shoeings and the visit notes for context.",
  "helpStepPhotos3": "Use the photo comparison view to place two photos from an animal's history side by side and track progress over time.",
  "helpStepPhotos4": "Add a caption to any photo to remember what it shows.",
  "helpSectionFindingTitle": "Finding Things",
  "helpStepFinding1": "Use the search field in the client picker to find a client quickly by name or address.",
  "helpStepFinding2": "The animal list screen shows every animal across all clients in one place.",
  "helpStepFinding3": "Last-visit badges on client and animal lists show how long it's been since their last appointment.",
  "helpStepFinding4": "The today route screen lists today's visits in order so you can plan your driving route.",
  "helpSectionBackupsTitle": "Backups",
  "helpStepBackups1": "Go to Settings and tap \"Create Backup\" to save a complete zip of your data and photos, ready to share or store somewhere safe.",
  "helpStepBackups2": "Back up regularly, especially before switching devices or clearing app storage.",
  "helpStepBackups3": "Tap \"Restore Backup\" and choose a backup zip file to restore — this replaces all current data on the device, so make sure you mean to overwrite it.",
  "helpStepBackups4": "Use \"Export Data\" for a CSV export of clients, animals, visits, service lines, and invoice summaries — handy for spreadsheets or accounting software.",
  "helpSectionOfflineTitle": "Working Offline",
  "helpStepOffline1": "FarrierLog stores everything locally on your device — there is no account, cloud sync, or internet connection required.",
  "helpStepOffline2": "You can add clients, schedule visits, take photos, and generate invoices anywhere, with or without signal.",
  "helpStepOffline3": "Because there's no cloud copy, your backups are the only way to move data to a new device or recover from data loss — back up before you need to.",
  "helpStepOffline4": "Sharing an invoice, backup, or export uses your device's normal share options (email, messaging, cloud drive), which do require a connection at that moment.",

